@startuml koda_cycle2_deployment_network
title Cycle 2 — Probleme d'adressage reseau (Raspberry Pi vs backend)

skinparam shadowing false

node "Reseau local\n(Wi-Fi robot)" as LAN {
  [Raspberry Pi\n192.168.x.x] as RPI
  [PC developpement\nlocalhost:8000] as PC
}

cloud "Hebergement backend\n(VPS / Docker)" as VPS {
  [Distributeur\napi.koda.example:443] as DS
}

node "Smartphone\n(emulateur / device)" as PH {
  [KodaMate Flutter] as APP
}

RPI -[#red,dashed]-> PC : **Conflit initial** :\nconfig pointe vers\nlocalhost ou IP obsolete
RPI -[#green]-> DS : **Solution** :\nURL publique ou IP LAN\ndu serveur backend
APP -[#orange,dashed]-> DS : **CORS** :\norigine mobile bloquee\nsi non whitelistee
APP -[#green]-> DS : **Solution** :\nCORSMiddleware +\norigines dev/prod

note bottom of RPI
  Le robot et le mobile doivent
  cibler la **meme** base URL backend,
  distincte de l'URL n8n (Cycle 1).
end note

@enduml
